.TH SDL_HINT_GAMECONTROLLER_SENSOR_FUSION 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_GAMECONTROLLER_SENSOR_FUSION \- A variable that controls whether the device\(aqs built-in accelerometer and gyro should be used as sensors for gamepads.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_GAMECONTROLLER_SENSOR_FUSION \(dqSDL_GAMECONTROLLER_SENSOR_FUSION\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Sensor fusion is disabled
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Sensor fusion is enabled for all controllers that lack sensors
.PP
Or the variable can be a comma separated list of USB VID/PID pairs in hexadecimal form, e\[char46]g\[char46]
.PP
0xAAAA/0xBBBB,0xCCCC/0xDDDD
.PP
The variable can also take the form of \(dq@file\(dq, in which case the named file will be loaded and interpreted as the value of the variable\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before a gamepad is opened\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

